nixarchy #1923: the shell's rescanPlugins() waits for a running scan check too.

CARRIED, quattro (edge) only: quattro's shell.qml has a rescanPlugins()
function that queues a rescan while a scan runs. With 1923-reaper-check.patch
a check can be running instead, so it tests `checking` as well. Omarchy v4.5.0
has no such function (its IPC rescanPlugins calls reloadPlugins, which
1923-reaper-check.patch already guards), so default.nix applies this only when
shell.qml has the shell-level rescanPlugins(). Drop it with 1923-reaper-check.patch.

Applied right after 1923-reaper-check.patch. --fuzz=0.

diff -ru a/shell/shell.qml b/shell/shell.qml
--- a/shell/shell.qml
+++ b/shell/shell.qml
@@ -1573,7 +1573,7 @@
   // plugin's panel (Superwhisper's setup) otherwise closed the menu and
   // blanked the wallpaper.
   function rescanPlugins() {
-    if (shell.pluginReloading || shell.pluginRegistry.scanning) {
+    if (shell.pluginReloading || (shell.pluginRegistry.scanning || shell.pluginRegistry.checking)) {
       shell.pluginRescanPending = true
       return
     }
